      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "This Game Brought To You By:\r\n    Dr. Meaghan Wetherell\r\n    Charles
    Scott\r\n    Atticus Birkett\r\n    Clovis Glasner\r\n    Gavin Lester\r\n   
    Ellie Martin\r\n    Evan Williams\r\n\r\n    From the University of Arizona\u2019s
    College of Information Science\r\n\r\n\r\nGame Designers, Developers & Artists\r\n\r   
    Lead Gameplay Programmer - Charlie Scott\r\n    Gameplay Programmer - Ellie Martin\r\n\r   
    3D Asset Creation - Gavin Lester  \r\n    3D Asset Creation - Evan Williams \r\n   
    3D Asset Creation - Dr. Meaghan Wetherell\r\n    3D Asset Creation - Clovis Glasner\r\n\r   
    UI Design - Atticus Birkett\r\n\r    Theme Music - Clovis Glasner\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nVoice
    Acting and Sound Effects\r\n    Narration - Dr. Meaghan Wetherell\r\n    Wii
    Sounds - Dennis Jenkins, Katlyn McDonough & the 2023 UO Archeology Field School
    \r\n    Footsteps recorded and edited by Dr. Meaghan Wetherell\r\n\r\n    Ambiance
    Wind Blowing Through Trees from Pixabay User Traian1984\r\n    Scale C6 from
    Pixabay User Leszek_Szary\r\n    American Pika Call and Ambiance from Acoustic
    Atlas User Jeff Rice\r\n\r\nModels\r\n    Barbed Wire Pack from Joey Carlino\r\n   
    Wire Fence from Pixel-bit\r\n    American Football House from DenWarden\r\n   
    Abandoned House from Sengchor\r\n    Barn Day 1 December 2022 Challenge from
    Eduard\r\n    Model 31a Timber Rattlesnake from DigitalLife3d\r\n    Bird nest
    in a wall from Matousekfoto\r\n    Winnemucca South Tufa Tower 1 by Laura\r\n\r\n\rBone
    models downloaded from Sketchfab and Morphosource, provided by:\r\n    Museum
    of Vertebrate Zoology\r\n    University of Michigan\u2019s Museum of Zoology
    Division of Mammals\r\n    Laboratory of Emma Sherratt\r\n    AMNH Mammal Collections\r\n   
    UMZC Zoological Specimens\r\n    Joseph Tyler at the Idaho Museum of Natural
    History\r\n    Nuttakorn Taewcharoen at the National Museum of Nature and Science,
    Tokyo\r\n    Fossils in Shropshire\r\n    Virtual Curation Lab\r\n    Erin Mein
    at the University of Queensland\u2019s School of Social Science     Archaeology
    Laboratories\r\n    Oxford University Museum of Natural History\r\n    University
    of Florida\u2019s Museum of Natural History\r\n    Mammals Collection of the
    Museum National d\u2019Histoire Naturelle\r\n    Kansas University\u2019s KUBI
    Mammalogy Collection\r\n\r\nShaders and Packages\r\n    Simple Water Shader URP
    by IgniteCoders  Version 1.0.0 \r\n\r\nSoftware\r\n    Unity was used as the
    game engine (3D, Universal Rendering Pipeline)\r\n    Materialize was used to
    develop normal maps from textures\r\n    Adobe Photoshop was used to create textures
    from images\r\n    Adobe Substance Painter was used to edit textures on 3D Models\r\n   
    Blender was used to create and edit 3D Models\r\n    Audacity was used for sound
    editing\r\n    Speedtree was used to create trees and plants\r\n\n\nFunding Provided
    By \r\n    National Science Foundation Award #2228632\r"
